 - If code outside of `macos/` directory is modified, use
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
 - Use `macos/build.nu` to build the macOS app, do not use `zig build`
   (except to build the underlying library as mentioned above).
   - Build: `macos/build.nu [--scheme Ghostty] [--configuration Debug] [--action build]`
-  - Output: `macos/build/<configuration>/Astrohacker Terminal.app` (e.g. `macos/build/Debug/Astrohacker Terminal.app`)
+  - Output: `macos/build/<configuration>/Astrohacker TermSurf.app` (e.g. `macos/build/Debug/Astrohacker TermSurf.app`)
 - Run unit tests directly with `macos/build.nu --action test`
 
 ## AppleScript
@@ -25,10 +25,10 @@
   (1) Build with `macos/build.nu`
   (2) Launch and activate the app via osascript using the absolute path
       to the built app bundle:
-      `osascript -e 'tell application "<absolute path to build/Debug/Astrohacker Terminal.app>" to activate'`
+      `osascript -e 'tell application "<absolute path to build/Debug/Astrohacker TermSurf.app>" to activate'`
   (3) Wait a few seconds for the app to fully launch and open a terminal.
   (4) Run test scripts with `osascript`, always targeting the app by
       its absolute path (not by name) to avoid calling the wrong
       application.
   (5) When done, quit via:
-      `osascript -e 'tell application "<absolute path to build/Debug/Astrohacker Terminal.app>" to quit'`
+      `osascript -e 'tell application "<absolute path to build/Debug/Astrohacker TermSurf.app>" to quit'`
